    "q-99661": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99661",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}{log}_{8}⁡(4-x)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{8}⁡(4-x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273970/assets/0b3cd9b5d4110b8b76b3e165d75ee4d8019cc9cc17192f38e9f2751350e5ddc7.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\ge 4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{+}}{log}_{8}⁡(4-x)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x<4.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {4}^{-}}{log}_{8}⁡(4-x)=-\\infty .\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
